cket which  costumers had lined with toxic  but flame killing asbestos fortunately  for producers  aston could waste all the cigars he  wanted to because dutch masters cigars  sponsored and supplied the show  songwriter vic mizzy specialized in  music for television  and he composed many tv theme songs  including two of the all-time  most memorable the ones for greenacres  and  the addams family now here's my idea  [Music]  the latter with its lightly menacing  organ riff and fun finger snaps  debuted with the 1964 television sitcom  iteration of the addams family  and the song or its motifs were used in  most every subsequent atoms project  as it became so associated with  franchise  the lyrics of the theme like a lot of  musical intros to high concept  60 sitcoms thoroughly explains the show  particularly how the atoms are creepy  kooky mysterious and spooky which mizzy  said he understood because he'd been  around for the show's development  i went with david levy to pick out the  props for the set  so i already knew what it was the creepy  and the cougar  when mizzy played the melody and did the  finger snaps which he says just  came to him it delighted levi and  network executives  the composer had such a handle on how  the song should represent the show  that the director hired to shoot the  opening sequence let mizzy take over  he directed the actor's finger snaps and  gave one direction  to actors john astin and carolyn jones  be  lackadaisical the 1991 movie the adams  family  pulled from the charles adams old new  yorker cartoons as well as the 1964-66  tv series  for example it had a gothic look and  macabre feel like the comics  and incorporated the famous theme song  and characters introduced on the  television series  the latter was a big problem for adam's  family tv  show rights holder david levy two months  after the film began its successful  theatrical run  levy sued paramount studios and orion  productions  for 50 million dollars according to the